# EasySplit — environment variables. Everything is OPTIONAL for local dev:
# with no env at all, the app runs fully mocked (demo OCR, local SQLite, no SMS).

# --- Receipt OCR (optional) ---
# With a key set, receipt photos are parsed by Claude vision (model: claude-opus-4-8).
# Without it, /api/receipts/parse returns an editable demo receipt.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Storage (optional overrides) ---
# DATA_DIR=./data              # uploads + SQLite live here (gitignored)
# DATABASE_FILE=./data/settle.db

# --- Twilio SMS (optional — see docs/TWILIO.md; the MVP mocks this locally) ---
# Point a Twilio phone number's "A message comes in" webhook at
#   https://<your-domain>/api/sms/inbound  (HTTP POST)
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=ACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token          # also used to fetch MMS media & validate signatures
# TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+15551234567
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://settle.example.com # used to build room links in SMS replies

# --- Deploy (Vercel + Supabase) ---
# Set these three in Vercel's Project Settings → Environment Variables to run on
# serverless Postgres + object storage. With DATABASE_URL set, the app uses
# Postgres (the schema auto-bootstraps on first request); unset, it falls back
# to local SQLite. Image uploads persist only when the two SUPABASE_* vars are
# also set — without them the demo + typed-receipt flows still work fine.
#
# DATABASE_URL — Supabase → Project Settings → Database → Connection string →
# "Transaction pooler" (port 6543). URL-encode the password if it has symbols.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#
# SUPABASE_URL — Supabase → Project Settings → API → Project URL.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — Supabase → Project Settings → API → service_role
# key (server-only secret; never expose to the browser). Enables Supabase
# Storage for uploads (public bucket "uploads", auto-created on first upload).
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# --- OCR spend controls ---
# Model for receipt OCR (default: claude-sonnet-5 — ~1-2¢/receipt; set to
# claude-opus-4-8 for maximum accuracy at ~3x the cost).
# OCR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# OCR_MODEL_STRONG=claude-opus-4-8   # escalation pass for hard receipts (auto-triggered)
# Built-in abuse guards (no config needed): OCR is rate-limited to 10/hour per
# IP, 5/hour per SMS number, and 60/hour globally; images are downscaled
# client-side before upload; output tokens are capped. Prepaid API credits
# (no auto-reload) are the hard ceiling — if they run out, the app falls back
# to manual item entry instead of breaking.
